@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: moves 2-6 of the main.go decomposition, each with its symbol inventory, seam, risk and proof
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go
' covers: internal/agentio/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/golden_test.go
'
' Overview and the four patterns: _spec/_plans/main-decomposition.puml
' Moves 0-5 are DONE: goldens, agentio, credentials, posture, backend/sandbox,
' backend/dockeregress. Only move 6 (internal/run) remains.
' Move 2 landed 2026-08-27: main.go 3505 -> 2960, internal/credentials 572 lines +
' 903 of tests, plan goldens BYTE-IDENTICAL. ProviderLookup moved with it — the plan
' did not list it, but it is the lookup every other function here takes, and leaving
' it behind would have split the seam in half.
'
' Move 3 landed 2026-08-27: main.go 2960 -> 2687, internal/posture 389 lines + 293
' of tests, posture-sbx/posture-docker goldens added, plan goldens BYTE-IDENTICAL.
' Two seams tightened rather than moved as-is, because moving them unchanged would
' have carried the defect into the new package:
'   * MCPGateway read PROVEO_SBX_MCP itself, making the ROW a second place the
'     decision was made. It now takes the decision and the var name as values.
'   * reportImageChoice PRINTED and returned. It is ResolveImageChoice(ref)
'     (chosen, isLocal) now, and the caller prints — a package that renders a
'     posture should not also be where output happens.
'
' Move 4 landed 2026-08-27: main.go 2687 -> 1828, internal/backend/sandbox 913
' lines, internal/backend 25, plan goldens BYTE-IDENTICAL.
'
' The plan's stated RISK understated it. runSandboxInput did not merely carry 16
' caller-resolved fields — it carried `params runParams`, the whole cobra struct,
' so the dependency closure was 98 declarations: essentially all of main.go. The
' extraction was impossible until that was cut. Input now holds the ELEVEN values
' the functions actually read (target image authVar shell clone extra roles
' bridges, plus evidence/forwards/sandboxAddonOn resolved by the caller), which
' collapsed the closure 98 -> 4 and is the shape move 6 generalises into RunSpec.
' That de-coupling was verified inert on its own before anything moved.
'
' Three of the last four crossed with sandbox (KeptLines, SaveState, Enabled).
' The fourth, agentExitError, is returned by BOTH backends and read by main to set
' proveo's exit code, so it became backend.ExitError in a new parent package. The
' Plan/Execute interface the plan names is deliberately NOT declared there yet:
' RunSpec arrives with move 6, and an interface written before its second
' implementer is a guess at the shape rather than a description of it.
'
' Two smaller displacements the plan did not list, both forced by the seam and
' both ratified by the operator rather than assumed:
'   * auth_hints.go moved to internal/credentials (it already imported it and
'     carried the credential-boundary SPEC header); only runSandbox called it.
'   * ensureSbx PROMPTED via provisionConfirm. It now takes confirm func(string)
'     bool, so a backend does not own a terminal prompt — and a test can drive
'     "operator declined" without faking a tty.
'
' Rejected for the hint: its own internal/credentials/hints package (the surface
' is not yet big enough to earn the split) and injecting it into sandbox.Input
' (28 fields already).
'
' Move 5 landed 2026-08-27: main.go 1826 -> 1615, internal/backend/dockeregress
' 276 lines, docker goldens BYTE-IDENTICAL.
'
' assembleInput carried `params runParams` exactly as runSandboxInput did; the
' same cut reduced move 5's closure to ONE symbol (waitForFile). Nine values:
' target image authVar mode credentials localModel dataDir shell extra.
'
' startReviewGate owned the terminal — ptyproxy over os.Stdin/os.Stdout,
' choiceui.Consent, tcell. It now takes consent func(host, port string) bool and
' cmd/proveo builds the overlay (reviewConsent). Operator-ratified, and the same
' shape as ensureSbx's confirm. The review tier is testable headless for the first
' time: a caller can pass deny-all and assert the decisions with no tty.
'
' The signal behaviour the plan called "the one no golden can see" is now covered
' by tests/e2e/signal_test.go — a REAL run, a REAL SIGINT, asserting no container
' or network carrying the session id survives. Chosen over a unit test of the
' sync.Once deliberately: the failure mode is defer and the handler RACING, which
' a fake cannot reproduce. It is opt-in (PROVEO_SIGNAL_TEST=1) because it needs
' docker and ~90s.
'
' ── WHERE THE 3311 LINES SIT TODAY (script over top-level declarations) ─────
'   move 2  credentials      411 lines / 23 decls
'   move 3  posture          184 lines / 13 decls
'   move 4  sandbox backend  756 lines / 24 decls
'   move 5  docker backend   223 lines /  8 decls
'   move 6  stages + cli    1092 lines / 24 decls   (doRun alone is 569)
'   helpers that follow their callers   594 lines / 55 decls
'
' Projected size of cmd/proveo/main.go after each move:
'   after 2 ~2900 · after 3 ~2716 · after 4 ~1960 · after 5 ~1737 · after 6 ~450
'
' ── MOVE 2 · internal/credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────
' WHAT: authSuppressor(40) agentTranscript(36) parseEnvFile(33) loginUsable(26)
'   loadedSecretNames(25) ghConfigMount(23) writeBrokerEnv(20) brokerProviders(19)
'   effectiveAuthVar(18) envAuthVars(18) warnMountedSecrets(17) providerForAuthVar(16)
'   brokerOffReason(16) reachableHosts(16) hasPersistedLogin losesToChosenAuth
'   oauthCredential hydrateProcessEnv configVarsFor providerOfKeyVar joinDomains
' SEAM: every one is a pure function of (manifest, lookup func(string) string,
'   homeRoot) — no run state, no cobra, no docker. That is why it goes first.
' RISK: writeBrokerEnv writes a real secret file; keep it the only writer and keep
'   its 0600. warnMountedSecrets prints, so it takes a ui writer rather than
'   reaching for the package global, or the posture tests cannot capture it.
' PROOF: existing unit tests move with it; the plan goldens do not change because
'   the argv these produce is unchanged. Add one test that the package NEVER
'   returns a value from lookup for a suppressed var.
'
' ── MOVE 3 · internal/posture ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' WHAT: observability(13) enforcedBy(7) imagePosture(8) workspacePosture(13)
'   mcpGatewayPosture(14) rolesLine(12) workspaceHeader(25) withGlyphs(22)
'   glyphMode/glyphModeFrom(16) detectHooks(19) reportImageChoice(18) mergeRoles(17)
' SEAM: one Posture value built once, rendered twice — the prompt header a human
'   reads before launch, and the runlog.Fields block a human reads after failure.
'   Today those two are assembled independently, which is how a row could name
'   Squid logs on a backend that runs none (fixed; the type prevents the class).
' RISK: the transcript's key order is asserted nowhere. Fix that here: the Fields
'   map becomes a struct with a stable render, and one golden covers it.
' PROOF: a posture golden per backend, beside the plan goldens.
'
' ── MOVE 4 · internal/backend/sandbox ───────────────────────────────────────
' WHAT: sandboxSpec(202) runSandbox(127) sbxHome(49) workspaceBinds(47)
'   kitCredentials(44) kitEnvVars(29) ensureSbx(28) sbxReady(23)
'   reportSbxUnavailable(23) captureSandboxPolicyLog(19) resolvedModelEnv(15)
'   withMCPGatewayPolicy(15) warnSandboxBaseline(14) declineMCPGateway
'   sbxStateHome sbxMCPGatewayAllowed willSandbox runSandboxInput firstHost
' SEAM: sandboxSpec is ALREADY the pure half and runSandbox already the impure
'   half — this move only gives that split a package boundary and a name. The
'   Backend interface is Plan(RunSpec) then Execute(Plan).
' RISK: runSandboxInput carries 16 fields, several resolved by cmd/proveo (memory,
'   homeRoot, gitEnv). They become RunSpec fields, resolved by move 6's stages —
'   until then the struct crosses the boundary unchanged.
' PROOF: sbx-*.golden must be byte-identical. They render RunArgs + the Kit + the
'   secret NAMES, which is the entire observable output of this package.
'
' ── MOVE 5 · internal/backend/dockeregress ──────────────────────────────────
' WHAT: execWithEgress(69) startReviewGate(44) assemble(38) captureSidecarLogs(23)
'   onSignalCleanup(14) reviewSupported(12) needsLifecycle(5) assembleInput(18)
' SEAM: same interface as move 4. After this, doRun SELECTS a backend instead of
'   branching on a bool that six other places also read.
' RISK: execWithEgress owns teardown, signal handling and the review gate. Its
'   cleanup must stay once-only (sync.Once) and must still run on SIGINT — the
'   one behaviour no golden can see. Keep its existing test and add a signal one.
' PROOF: docker-*.golden byte-identical; the egress integration suite green
'   (PROVEO_EGRESS_INTEGRATION=1 -tags=integration).
'
' ── MOVE 6 · internal/run · the stages ──────────────────────────────────────
' WHAT: doRun(569) splits into named stages over one RunSpec:
'   resolveWorkspace · resolveCredentials · promptChoices · buildPosture ·
'   selectBackend · execute · teardown
'   promptChoices(64) gateAddons(46) gateReview(37) gateEvidence(18)
'   addonOptions(22) applyCapabilities(18) seedFromCache(17) go to
'   internal/run/choices.go beside them; runCmd(74) main(48) doSetup(46)
'   projectsCmd(20) stay in cmd/proveo as wiring.
' SEAM: each stage takes RunSpec and returns a value or an error; the executor
'   applies effects. --print stops being a branch and becomes "stop after plan".
' RISK: the highest of the six. doRun's locals are its hidden contract — sid,
'   egDir, uid/gid, mounts, workdir, lookup, detected, homePlan. Enumerate them
'   into RunSpec BEFORE splitting, in one commit that changes nothing else.
' PROOF: every golden, both integration and the e2e ladder. This is the move that
'   most needs the e2e baseline green first — see _spec/_plans/restore-green-e2e.
title moves 2 to 6 — 2 through 5 DONE, only move 6 remains

component "cmd/proveo/main.go\n3311 lines today · 158 declarations" as MAIN <<error>>

frame "the five remaining moves, in order" as MOVES <<host>> {
  component "**2 · internal/credentials** ✅ DONE\n572 lines — pure over manifest + lookup" as M2 <<db>>
  component "**3 · internal/posture** ✅ DONE\n389 lines — one value, two readers" as M3 <<db>>
  component "**4 · backend/sandbox** ✅ DONE\n913 lines — the pure/impure split, named" as M4 <<db>>
  component "**5 · backend/dockeregress** ✅ DONE\n276 lines — same interface, second impl" as M5 <<db>>
  component "**6 · internal/run** DONE\ndoRun 595 -> Do 55 over seven stages" as M6 <<app>>
}

frame "what proves each move inert" as PROOF <<host>> {
  component "plan goldens\ndocker-*.golden · sbx-*.golden" as G <<db>>
  component "posture golden ✅\nposture-sbx · posture-docker" as PG <<db>>
  component "egress integration\nreal Squid + MITM + broker mount" as INT <<app>>
  component "e2e baseline\nmust be green before move 6" as E2E <<error>>
}

MAIN ARROW_MAIN M2
M2 ARROW_MAIN M3
M3 ARROW_MAIN M4
M4 ARROW_MAIN M5
M5 ARROW_MAIN M6

M2 ARROW_QUEUE G
M3 ARROW_QUEUE PG
M4 ARROW_QUEUE G
M5 ARROW_QUEUE INT
M6 ARROW_OPTIONAL E2E : same 5 reds before and after

note bottom of M2
  First because it depends on nothing else in the
  run: manifest in, lookup in, a decision out. It
  is also where the .env and the broker file live,
  so one package owns every path a secret takes.
end note

note bottom of M4
  The cheapest of the four extractions: the pure
  half and the effect half already exist as two
  functions. This move gives them a package and an
  interface, and moves no logic between them.
end note

note bottom of M6
  Done. Spec was enumerated first as an inert
  change, then the body sliced. Stage names and
  order differ from the plan where OUTPUT ORDER
  forced it.
  See _spec/internal/run/run-spec.puml.
end note

note bottom of E2E
  C1 was a MISDIAGNOSIS of the seed abort fixed
  separately: 8 red -> 5 red with no C1 change.
  Move 6 was judged on a before/after of those 5
  plus a new golden over the resolve path, which
  the plan goldens never covered.
end note
@enduml
